  "note": "undefined The stepped digests were re-recorded from the kernels at body-genes T7: the pooled-v6 layout changes what a random brain does, so every stepped world moves; the fuzz digests do not depend on the layout and are unchanged. Re-recorded again at body-genes T31, when pooling started reading the body sense lanes and every stepped world moved. Stepped digests re-recorded from the Rust kernels when a startled herd stopped holding its centroid (role-budget T21a, `summarizeGroup`): the herds move differently in every busy world, and the cases that moved are named in docs/notes/2026-11.md. Stepped digests re-recorded for smoke dropped toward a hunter in front (feat(sim)!: smokeAimArc): a world where a releaser has a hunter ahead drops its cloud elsewhere. Stepped digests re-recorded again when the smoke aim moved from a scan of every agent to the nearest threat on the releaser's own rays (perf/smoke-aim-local-sensing): a releaser aims along a ray, not at the hunter's bearing. Stepped digests re-recorded for the smoke decoy (feat(sim)!: smokeDecoyTicks): a fresh cloud also reads on the prey channel, so a hunter whose rays meet a cloud sees a body in it."
}
